.\" -*- mode: troff; coding: utf-8 -*-
.TH AMU\-SRC 8
.SH NAME
amu\-src \- build Qwaderton Linux packages from source recipes
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
\fBamu\-src\fR builds \fI.spm\fR packages from \fIabuild\fR recipes, in
the role of a makepkg-style source build tool. It reads a recipe (a
POSIX shell snippet defining the package name, version, sources and
optional build hooks), downloads and verifies source tarballs,
auto-detects one of the supported build systems, compiles the software,
post-processes the result (compresses man pages, strips binaries,
removes static libraries, locales and documentation, installs runit
services), and packages the fakeroot into an \fI.spm\fR archive.
.LP
\fBamu\-src\fR never modifies the target system and never invokes
\fBspm\fR(8) directly: packaging is delegated to \fBamu\-bin \-b\fR, and
installation (with \fB\-i\fR/\fB\-u\fR) is delegated to \fBamu\-bin\fR(8)
after a successful build. Recipe metadata, searching and dependency
resolution are shared with \fBamu\-bin\fR(8) through the recipe
repositories synchronized by \fBreposync\fR(8).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR [\fIpkg...\fR]
Build and install. With no arguments, builds the recipe in the current
directory; with arguments, builds each named package found in
\fBAMU_REPO\fR. The built package is handed to \fBamu\-bin \-i\fR.
The recipe's \fIpreinstall\fR script runs before the build; the
\fIpostinstall\fR script and system triggers run on the \fBamu\-bin\fR
side after installation.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR [\fIpkg...\fR]
Rebuild and upgrade. Like \fB\-i\fR, but hands the package to
\fBamu\-bin \-u\fR; refuses if the package is not installed.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR
Force rebuild even if the package file already exists.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR [\fIpkg...\fR]
Download source tarballs only.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR \fI<pkg...>\fR
Print the recipe directory path of each package.
.TP
\fB\-g\fR [\fIpkg...\fR]
Regenerate the \fI.shasum\fR checksum file.
.TP
\fB\-k\fR [\fIpkg...\fR]
Regenerate the \fI.files\fR package file list.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR [\fIpattern\fR]
Search packages in the recipe repositories. With \fB\-v\fR, prints name
and version.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Verbose output (with \fB\-s\fR).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR
Print help and exit.

.SH RECIPES
.LP
A recipe lives in a directory named after the package and contains an
\fIabuild\fR file defining at least:
.RS
.nf

name=mypkg
version=1.2.3
release=1
source="https://example.com/$name-$version.tar.gz"

.fi
.RE
.LP
The \fIsource\fR variable accepts remote URLs, \fIname::url\fR renames,
\fIurl::noextract\fR markers, local files, and may be empty for dummy
packages. Optional variables: \fIbuild_opt\fR, \fIbuild_type\fR (force a
build system), \fIbuild_dir\fR, \fIsv\fR (runit services),
\fIskip_patch\fR, \fIpatch_opt\fR, \fIkeep_static\fR, \fIkeep_libtool\fR,
\fIkeep_locale\fR, \fIkeep_doc\fR, \fIno_strip\fR, \fIsafely_rebuildable\fR.
.LP
A \fBbuild()\fR function in the recipe replaces the auto-detected build
system entirely; otherwise \fBprebuild()\fR and \fBpostbuild()\fR hooks
run around it. When the version is unchanged and the recipe sets
\fIsafely_rebuildable\fR, a \fBrebuild()\fR function runs instead of a
full rebuild.
.LP
Companion files: \fIdepends\fR (runtime dependencies, one per line),
\fImakedepends\fR (build-time dependencies), \fIinfo\fR (metadata),
\fIpreinstall\fR, \fIpostinstall\fR, \fI.shasum\fR (source checksums),
\fI.files\fR (package file list). See \fBamu-resolv\fR(8) for how
dependencies are resolved.
.LP
Build systems are auto-detected in this order: \fBmeson.build\fR (muon),
\fBconfigure\fR, \fBCMakeLists.txt\fR, \fBsetup.py\fR, \fBMakefile.PL\fR,
\fBMakefile\fR. The exact flags are documented in the package
documentation under \fI/usr/share/doc/amutils\fR.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBAMU_REPO\fR
Space-separated recipe repository directories (required for named
package operations and \fB\-s\fR).
.TP
\fBAMU_PACKAGE_DIR\fR
Directory for built \fI.spm\fR files (default: current directory).
.TP
\fBAMU_SOURCE_DIR\fR
Source tarball cache directory (default: current directory).
.TP
\fBAMU_WORK_DIR\fR
Build working tree, extraction and fakeroot location (default: current
directory).
.TP
\fBAMU_ROOT\fR
Alternative install root, passed through to \fBamu\-bin\fR.
.TP
\fBAMU_NOPROMPT\fR
Skip the \fBamu\-bin\fR confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fBAMU_KEEP_WORKDIR\fR
Keep the build tree on failure (for debugging).
.TP
\fBAMU_LOG\fR, \fBAMU_LOG_DIR\fR
Enable build logging; log file is \fI$AMU_LOG_DIR/$name.log\fR.
.TP
\fBCFLAGS\fR, \fBCXXFLAGS\fR
Compiler flags (used by the cmake build system).
.TP
\fBCROSS_COMPILE\fR
Toolchain prefix for \fBstrip\fR (e.g. \fIx86_64-linux-musl-\fR).

.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/etc/amu.conf\fR
System-wide configuration, sourced by the amu library.

